The feature I'd prioritize most
If you want NovelVerse to stand out, I wouldn't start by trying to build every social feature above.
I'd build this specific loop exceptionally well:
Share a novel → Create Reading Room → Invite friends → Set chapters → Everyone reads independently → Chapter discussion unlocks after completion → Reactions/comments → Vote for next chapter/book → Continue together.
That gives NovelVerse a genuine identity:
Netflix makes watching stories together easy. NovelVerse makes reading stories together easy.

And it fits perfectly with your desktop-first approach: the novel reader on one side + friends/discussion/progress panel on the other can become one of the platform's signature UI experiences.